  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-21T06:12:58.946Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I’ve noticed people keep inviting Quest users to PC-Only worlds, either directly or by accepting a join request. This causes the Quest user to attempt and join before being kicked home with no explanation.\nIt is quite annoying, so I suggest that you should not be allowed to accept or invite someone if they are on an unsupported platform. World is hidden sometimes before being invited, so making it so the Quest player also gets a prompt when attempting to join would be nice.\nEither way, I dislike accepting an invite just to get kicked to my home world. It should not allow me to accept nor them to send an invite if the other is on an unsupported platform for that world.\n(it would also be nice if instead of being kicked home, we were sent back to the previous instance)",
